# Responsive UI / UX (mobile, tablet, desktop)

Build every screen **mobile-first** with Tailwind. It must work at three widths. Do not add custom breakpoints.

| Band | Width | Classes |
|------|--------|---------|
| Mobile | under 768px | default (no prefix). Sidebar is a sheet via `useIsMobile` (768). |
| Tablet | 768–1023px | `md:` |
| Desktop | 1024px and up | `lg:` and up |

`sm:` (640px) is only for small phone tweaks (full-width buttons, stacked toolbars).

## Layout

- Page headers: `flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between`.
- Forms and filters: `grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`.
- Primary actions: `w-full sm:w-auto`. Controls at least `h-10`; do not shrink tap targets on mobile.
- Inputs, selects, and date controls stay `w-full` until `md:`.
- Tables: from `md:` keep the table. Below `md:`, use a stacked card list, or wrap in `overflow-x-auto` on a `min-w-0` parent. The page must not scroll sideways.
- Dialogs / sheets: near full width on mobile (`w-[calc(100%-2rem)]`), then existing max width (`sm:max-w-lg` or larger) from tablet up.
- Spacing: prefer `gap-3` / `p-4` on mobile; increase only when the layout needs air at `md:` / `lg:`.
- Long text: `min-w-0` on flex children, plus `truncate` or `break-words`.

## Interaction & UX

- Primary actions stay visible without hover. Mobile and tablet have no reliable hover — do not hide critical actions in hover-only menus.
- A sidebar that stays open on `lg:` must use the existing sheet sidebar below `md:`.
- Shorten labels on small screens with `hidden sm:inline` / `sm:hidden` when the full label will not fit. Do not drop the action.
- Prefer one clear primary CTA per toolbar/section; secondary actions can collapse into a menu on mobile if needed.
- Touch-friendly: avoid tiny icon-only hit areas; use `size="icon"` buttons with adequate padding, or pair icons with text on larger screens.
- Focus and keyboard: keep focus rings; do not remove outline for “cleaner” mobile UI.

## Do not

- Fixed widths that overflow phones (`w-[480px]`, rigid multi-column rows without stacking).
- Desktop-only horizontal toolbars that wrap awkwardly or clip on tablet.
- Relying on hover, dual-click, or dense data grids as the only way to complete a task on mobile.
- Adding custom media queries or new breakpoint tokens unless the design system already has them.

## Examples

```tsx
// BAD — fixed desktop row, overflows a phone
<div className="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
  <Button className="w-[180px]">Save</Button>
</div>

// GOOD
<div className="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
  <Button className="w-full sm:w-auto">Save</Button>
</div>
```

When layout changes, check ~390px (mobile), 768px (tablet), and 1280px (desktop).
